<title>USA: Perkin-Elmer, Spectro end purchase talks.</title>
<headline>Perkin-Elmer, Spectro end purchase talks.</headline>
<dateline>NORWALK, Conn. 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Perkin-Elmer Corp said on Friday that it and Spectro Gesellschaft fur Spektrometrie GmbH &amp; Co have discontinued negotiations about the possible acquisition of Spectro by Perkin-Elmer's analytical instruments division.</p>
<p>The companies gave no reason for ending the talks, but said they agreed to discuss future cooperative arrangements.</p>
<p>Spectro, of Kleve, Germany, is involved in arc-light spectrometry for analysis of solids.</p>
<p>Perkin-Elmer makes life-science systems and analytical instruments.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
